.TH SKOGAI-CONFIG-UNSET 1  "skogai-config-unset 0.0.0" 
.SH NAME
skogai\-config\-unset \- remove a key from the local layer, the global one, a module's module.local.md or a \-\-file's .local.md
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskogai config unset\fR [OPTIONS] <KEY>
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-global\fR
.br
remove from the global layer instead of local
.TP
\fB\-\-module\fR=\fIMODULE\fR
.br
remove from this module's module.local.md
.TP
\fB\-\-file\fR=\fIFILE\fR
.br
remove from this file's .local.md frontmatter instead
.TP
\fB\-\-scope\fR=\fISCOPE\fR
.br
the section \-\-file keys are mounted under
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.br
Print help
.TP
<\fIKEY\fR>

.SH "ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES:"
.TP
\fISKOGAI_SYSTEM_DIR\fR [default: /etc/skogai]
.br
dir of the system layer config
.TP
\fISKOGAI_CONFIG_DIR\fR
.br
dir of the global layer, default ~/.config/skogai
.TP
\fISKOGAI_LOCAL_DIR\fR [default: .skogai]
.br
dir of the local layer; relative is from the git root, or pwd
.TP
\fISKOGAI_MODULE_PATH\fR
.br
colon\-separated dirs of module sources, default the one this module sits in
